From 0c8e2d20f9a2f308b662e08a6d5675b5c57bffde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: royka1 <397414+royka1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:58:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 87/88] wifi: ath11k: Use the nfa765 firmware on the Xiaomi 12T
 Pro

The Xiaomi 12T Pro (diting) has a QCA6490 (WCN6855 hw2.1) with board
data in the ELF format of Qualcomm's mobile designs. The default WCN6855
firmware (WLAN.HSP.1.1-03125 SILICONZ_LITE) does not accept the phone's
board data: the board data download times out, so only the generic
board-id-255 entry of board-2.bin can be used, which carries the RF
configuration of a different design. With it the phone finds no 5 GHz
networks at all and uses a single stream on 2.4 GHz.

The nfa765 firmware (WLAN.HSP.1.1-04685 SILICONZ_IOE), already selected
for Qualcomm's QCA6490 evaluation boards, loads the phone's board data.
The firmware Android runs on this phone (WLAN.HSP.2.0.c2, not in
linux-firmware) also boots under ath11k and receives on both chains in
both bands; it can be installed into the nfa765 directory under
updates/, with linux-firmware's nfa765 files as the fallback.

Device-tested on the Xiaomi 12T Pro (firmware loaded through
firmware_class.path first, then this patch).

Signed-off-by: royka1 <397414+royka1@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
index 8dacc878c..f5597ce93 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
@@ -1052,6 +1052,7 @@ static const struct __ath11k_core_usecase_firmware_table {
 	{ ATH11K_HW_WCN6855_HW21, "qcom,lemans-evk", "nfa765"},
 	{ ATH11K_HW_WCN6855_HW21, "qcom,monaco-evk", "nfa765"},
 	{ ATH11K_HW_WCN6855_HW21, "qcom,hamoa-iot-evk", "nfa765"},
+	{ ATH11K_HW_WCN6855_HW21, "xiaomi,diting", "nfa765"},
 	{ /* Sentinel */ }
 };
 
